// How much the bar range is expanding against its own recent expansion, summed
// over a window.
//
// Exercises three warmups stacked: a smoothing of the range, a smoothing of
// that, and a window over the ratio of the two. Each one starts counting at its
// input's first value rather than at bar 0, which is why the reading lands two
// smoothings and a window deep.

version 1

study("Mass expansion", overlay = false, precision = 4)

len = input(10, "Sum length", min = 1, max = 500)

// The two smoothing lengths are part of the definition of the study rather than
// settings, so neither is an input.
smoothLen = 9

reach  = high - low
single = ema(reach, smoothLen)
double = ema(single, smoothLen)

// A market flat long enough for the smoothed range to reach zero has no
// expansion to measure, and nothing is the honest answer there.
ratio = double == 0 ? none : single / double

plot(sum(ratio, len), "Mass", blue, width = 2)
